;; ===========================================================================
;; Public-API manifest — CURATED metadata sidecar (rf2-3nbl5.2).
;;
;; This file is the human-curated half of the public-API manifest's
;; single-source design. The generator
;; (implementation/scripts/api-manifest/) derives EXISTENCE + :kind +
;; :facade? from live public vars; it joins those against the
;; :classification map here for the three human-classification axes that
;; cannot be derived from code:
;;
;;   :tier   — the closed Tier vocabulary (spec/API.md §Tier taxonomy):
;;             :front-porch | :advanced | :tooling | :adapter | :testing
;;             | :internal-public | :deprecated. Restrictive-by-default:
;;             when ambiguous, pick the MORE restrictive tier.
;;   :owner  — the canonical owning Spec doc (e.g. "002", "Tool-Pair",
;;             "009", "007") — the "where does the contract live" anchor.
;;   :status — shipping lineage (spec/API.md §Conventions Status).
;;
;; HAND-EDIT THIS FILE; never hand-edit spec/api-manifest.edn (generated).
;; Adding a public var? Add its [namespace var] entry here, then
;; regenerate. The CI drift-check (lint.yml → api-manifest job) goes red
;; until both this sidecar and the generated manifest are updated.
;;
;; The :classification map is keyed by ["namespace" "var"] (both strings).
;; ===========================================================================
{:meta
 {:doc      "Curated tier/owner/status sidecar for the public-API manifest."
  :keystone "rf2-3nbl5.2"}

